<title>JAPAN: Yaohan sags on redemption problem report.</title>
<headline>Yaohan sags on redemption problem report.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Yaohan Japan Corp sagged on Friday as investors sold the shares on worries sparked by a newspaper report stating that the supermarket operator may be short of funds to redeem convertible bonds (CBs), brokers said.</p>
<p>Yaohan later denied the reports, saying that it will use cash, inventories and loans to redeem them.</p>
<p>As of 0440 GMT, the shares were down 28 yen or 8.33 percent at 308 and were the largest percentage loser on the first section of the Tokyo bourse.</p>
